## The split, stated before the test list

The PRD tags every phase-3 criterion [manual], [manual, device] or [static];
the plan's TDD routing says so and names the single decidable slice this
phase adds — the sheet's state machine, extracted to
`src/shared/task-sheet.ts` exactly so the "draft kept in memory", "close
without deleting" and "saved drops the draft" rules could be tested without
a `<dialog>` (`docs/context/methodology.md`, "split the logic out, then the
glue is exempt"). The dialog primitive, the fields, the requests, the token
gate and the playground are React glue, verified by the plan's own VALIDATE
probes, the browser pane and the owner's phone. The diff a save sends is
`buildTaskPatch`, already pinned by `test/task-edit.test.ts` and consumed
unchanged — not duplicated here.

## Test files written this session

- `test/task-sheet.test.ts` — 24 cases in eight `describe` blocks against the
  new pure `src/shared/task-sheet.ts` (plan Task 1, AC-A8):
  - **`draftFromTask`** — an undated, unprioritised Task seeds *Sem data*
    with empty text fields; a deadline seeds *Concluir até* with the date,
    keeping description and priority; a scheduled date seeds *Fazer em*.
  - **initial state and `currentDraft`** — the initial state is closed, in
    the detail view, with no draft; `currentDraft` returns the kept draft
    object itself, or a fresh seed when none is kept.
  - **`open`** — opens in the detail view and seeds the draft; restores a
    kept draft untouched (same object) instead of re-seeding — the AC-12
    rule; keeps other Tasks' drafts; always lands in the detail view.
  - **`edit`** — merges changes and keeps the other fields; accepts clearing
    the priority; never touches a Task that is not open; no-op while closed.
  - **`request-delete` / `cancel-delete`** — the view switches to
    `confirm` and back to `detail` with the very same draft; both no-ops
    while closed.
  - **`close`** — clears the Task and the view, keeps the same drafts
    object; a close from the confirmation closes without deleting; no-op
    when already closed.
  - **`saved` / `deleted`** — drop that Task's draft and close; a reopen
    after `saved` seeds from the updated Task; `deleted` keeps the other
    drafts.
  - **purity** — frozen state, drafts and changes are never mutated.

